<title>USA: FORECAST-Price war to trim oil company Q4 earnings.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Price war to trim oil company Q4 earnings.</headline>
<byline>James Pierpoint</byline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fourth quarter earnings for oil companies operating on the U.S. West Coast were expected to fall victim to a gasoline price war waged in Los Angeles late last year, analysts said.</p>
<p>The weaker marketing margins resulting from lower gasoline prices will offset an otherwise banner year-end quarter for domestic oil companies, which benefitted from steadily rising crude oil prices and improved refining margins, analysts said.</p>
</text>
